        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='width:100%;min-height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;container-type:inline-size;background:#ffffff;font-family:Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,5cqw,40px) 64px'><div style='padding-top:32px'><header data-role='masthead'><div style='padding:10px 0;border-top:3px solid #0f172a;border-bottom:1px solid #0f172a;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>PRIMITIVE · content</div><h1 style='margin:40px 0 0;font:500 clamp(40px,9.5cqw,72px)/.98 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em;text-wrap:balance;color:#0f172a'>Content</h1><p style='margin:18px 0 0;max-width:36ch;font:italic 400 clamp(20px,3.6cqw,26px)/1.35 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#475569'>Durable material that a View, or any other reader, can show.</p></header></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start;gap:32px 40px'><div style='flex:999 1 380px;min-width:0'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Meaning</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><span style='float:left;padding:6px 10px 0 0;font:500 68px/54px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#0f172a'>D</span>urable material that a View or another reader can consume. Encoding: a <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>content</code> node with a typed payload, independent of how many presentations use it.</p></section></div><div style='flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0'><section data-role='settings' style='padding-top:10px;border-top:3px solid #0f172a'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f172a'>At a glance</h2><dl style='margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr;column-gap:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #cbd5e1'><dt style='padding:9px 0 9px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Node type</dt><dd style='margin:0;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;text-align:right;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>content</dd><dt style='padding:9px 0 9px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Shown when browsing</dt><dd style='margin:0;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;text-align:right;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>Yes</dd><dt style='grid-column:1/-1;padding:9px 0 0px;border-top:1px solid #cbd5e1;font:400 13px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Encoded as</dt><dd style='grid-column:1/-1;margin:0;padding:2px 0 9px;font:600 14px/20px system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>a content node with a typed payload, independent of how many presentations use it</dd></dl></section></div></div></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Invariants</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Content preserves its material value; choosing a View does not rewrite it. Graph identity remains on the Declaration. Legacy readers are compatibility behavior, not the format new authors should prefer.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Contract</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Write <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.content = { kind, value }</code>. The current reader accepts markdown, html, svg, canvas, text, json and image. Image values may be a source string or an object with src/alt/fit; canvas uses an object payload. JSON values are stringified for preview. Unknown kinds fall back to text. Older direct fields and renderShape are read for compatibility; new authoring uses content.kind/value.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Ports and Relationships</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>A View delegates through an outgoing <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>surface-delegate</code> relationship to Content. The reader also accepts <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>view.content</code>/<code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>content</code> role aliases and legacy <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>data.sourceNodeId</code>. The first matching relationship selects the delegated material. Content does not own the Surface chain.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Behavior</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>resolveContentPayload</code> normalizes the payload; <code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>resolveViewContent</code> finds delegated material. ContentNode and ViewContentPayload render the supported material through the existing payload renderers. A View may instead own its own data.content.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Known gaps</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The previous plan listed only six kinds; the payload normalizer also recognizes canvas. This spec documents all seven without promoting canvas rendering into a new semantic primitive. Browser rendering and external image delivery are separate from payload normalization tests.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Renderer boundary: The content normalizer and inline preview mapper recognize canvas, but ContentNode and ViewContentPayload currently use a fallback textual preview rather than a dedicated canvas renderer. Accepting a payload kind in the normalizer does not prove every View host has a dedicated renderer for it.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Representations</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>One Content value can have several Views. Material kind selects a payload renderer; Surface and View selection choose the presentation. A selected representation uses the existing workspace frame. Surface and resolution changes do not implicitly resize it, reflow neighbors or change camera zoom. Focusing a graph draws it at its own authored size, whatever size it was dragged to in the workspace while it was not focused; that workspace size is kept for when focus leaves and never changes the graph. Manual resizing is explicit: on a focused graph it sets the graph’s own window, on an unfocused one only its size in this workspace. Internal nodes, edges, handles and pointer targets are clipped; exposed boundary controls remain accessible. Workspace title bars belong to View representations (including glyph-shaped artwork), not a terminal Glyph.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Not a Surface, not a View, and not graph identity. A markdown or svg legacy node is not the recommended new encoding.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Examples</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The linked example is a separate graph. Inspect its relevant nodes and relationships; this specification does not embed or execute the example.</p><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>The Page Template demonstrates material, presentation and behavior as separate authored nodes.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:48px'><section data-role='section'><h2 style='margin:0 0 14px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Where this lives</h2><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Source (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/utils/contentPayload.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/Nodes/ContentNode.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>components/GraphEditor/Nodes/ViewNode.js</code></li><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/contentPayload.test.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>Focused tests (twilite repository):</p><ul style='margin:0 0 14px;padding-left:22px;max-width:60ch;font:400 18px/1.55 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'><li style='margin:0 0 6px'><code style='padding:1px 4px;border-radius:3px;background:#f1f5f9;font:400 .84em ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere'>tests/viewOwnContentPortal.test.js</code></li></ul><p style='margin:0 0 14px;max-width:60ch;font:400 19px/1.6 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#1e293b'>These pointers identify evidence to inspect. Structural validation does not prove runtime or browser behavior.</p></section></div><div style='padding-top:40px'><div style='display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:stretch;gap:28px 32px'><div style='flex:1 1 190px;min-width:0'><section data-role='route' data-prominence='primary' style='height:100%;box-sizing:border-box;display:flex;flex-direction:column;padding-top:12px;border-top:3px solid #6d28d9'><h2 style='margin:0 0 8px;font:500 26px/1.1 Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#0f172a'>Page Template</h2><p style='margin:0 0 10px;font:400 14px/1.55 system-ui;color:#475569'>A worked example: templates/page-template.</p><a data-role='route-link' href='tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/root.node' style='margin-top:auto;font:700 13px/20px system-ui;text-decoration:none;color:#6d28d9'>Open the example →</a></section></div></div></div></div></div>"
        },
